{
  "id": "behavioral-rehearsal",
  "term": "behavioral rehearsal",
  "definition": "Behavioral rehearsal is a role-playing technique in psychotherapy in which a therapist guides a person to act out situations or roles so they can practice new ways of behaving. It is used to help strengthen change by trying out responses in action rather than only talking about them.",
